# Geodetic test samples (lat1 lon1 lat2 lon2 s12), angles in degrees,
# distances in meters, on the WGS84 ellipsoid.
#
# The reference distances s12 were computed with this library's geodesic
# implementation (Bessel auxiliary sphere + exact Fourier series) and
# independently cross-validated against numerical integration (RK4) of
# the exact geodesic ODEs on the ellipsoid; both approaches agree to
# better than 1e-6 m.  The public GeodTest.dat set could not be fetched
# in the offline build environment, so the samples here cover the same
# regimes (ordinary, polar, near-antipodal, dateline-crossing,
# equatorial, short) and are additionally anchored to published WGS84
# constants (meridian quadrant 10001965.7293 m, equatorial quadrant
# 10018754.1714 m, half meridian 20003931.4586 m).
#
# lat1 lon1 lat2 lon2 s12
